NAME

ulibFileNameAddress - Converts a packet filename to a FidoNet address


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibFileNameAddress(UBYTE *Name, struct FidoNetAddress *Fido)
                               a0                  a1


DESCRIPTION

This function converts a file name of the format Zone.Net.Node.Point.* to
a (struct FidoNetAddress).

Note that there must NOT be a path or directory prefix; this routine wants
only Zone.Net.Node.Point.* (for example, 1.250.642.0.FLO).  Any characters
may follow the point number, as long as the character immediately following
the point number is not a digit.


RETURNS

0        - Success
Non-zero - Failure

              1 - Missing zone
              2 - Missing net
              3 - Missing node
